ain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/pulls/6347","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/pull/6347","diff_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/pull/6347.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/pull/6347.patch","merged_at":"2022-05-03T07:45:15Z"},"body":"<!--\r\nThank you for submitting a PR to pylint!\r\n\r\nTo ease the process of reviewing your PR, do make sure to complete the following boxes.\r\n\r\n- [ ] Add a ChangeLog entry describing what your PR does.\r\n- [ ] If it's a new feature, or an important bug fix, add a What's New entry in\r\n      `doc/whatsnew/<current release.rst>`.\r\n- [ ] Write a good description on what the PR does.\r\n- [ ] If you used multiple emails or multiple names when contributing, add your mails\r\n   and preferred name in ``script/.contributors_aliases.json``\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## Type of Changes\r\n\r\n<!-- Leave the corresponding lines for the applicable type of change: -->\r\n\r\n|     | Type                   |\r\n| --- | ---------------------- |\r\n| ✓   | :bug: Bug fix          |\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nWith a suppressed `wrong-import-position` warning and `useless-suppressions` enabled, Pylint was issuing a `useless-suppression` warning even though the suppression was not useless. This was happening because of a change [here](https://github.com/PyCQA/pylint/commit/4f5d2279ca3694ea363ac5a1df54ecbdba2b612d) that fixed #1366; It was skipping the entire calculation of the checker when the warning was disabled, which prevents it from recording that the checker would have been hit. There's [a similar fix here](https://github.com/PyCQA/pylint/pull/5063/files) for the same case with `wrong-import-order`.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nIf this PR fixes a particular issue, use the following to automatically close that issue\r\nonce this PR gets merged:\r\n-->\r\n\r\nCloses #5219\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylin